dydo/project/decisions/003-agent-messaging.md:28:**Chosen:** Block the tool call (exit 2; **superseded by LC-1021, dydo 3.4.1:** a hook-mode block now exits 0 with a `deny` object on stdout, see [Guard System](../../understand/guard-system.md)) with a notification message. The agent is forced to acknowledge the message because it can't proceed. The notification explicitly tells the agent their tool call was valid but paused, and to retry after reading. This reuses the `UnreadMustReads` pattern - an `UnreadMessages` list in agent state, cleared when the message file is read via the Read tool. Dydo bash commands are exempt from the block so the agent can run `inbox show` and `inbox clear`.
